o at least one epic; no orphaned requirements.\n62\t\n63\t## Priority-Split Analysis\n64\t\n65\tHLR-3 (P2, CSV export) was evaluated for splitting from the P1 report work and\n66\tkept bundled — see the flagged matrix row above. HLR-1 and HLR-2 are one logical\n67\tchange (the strategy frames a single per-project idle/stale resource reporting\n68\tcapability in one console surface, and the export feature spans both reports),\n69\tso they share one epic rather than being split by report. HLR-4 is split out by\n70\twork-product type (content authoring vs. code), not by priority.\n71\t\n72\t## Investigation Epics\n73\t\n74\tNone. The strategy declares \"Open Questions: None\" and contains no risks,\n75\tassumptions, pending reviews, or conditional ADRs. The one latent unknown — the\n76\texact console-readable surface for the notebook controller's last-activity data\n77\t— is API-surface discovery the implementing team resolves when starting the\n78\twork; per the implementation-detail handling it is captured as an acceptance\n79\tcriterion on E001, with the expansion risk recorded under Health Warnings.\n80\t\n81\t## Health Warnings\n82\t\n83\t- **Missing strategy sections**: no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no Non-Functional Requirements. Decomposition proceeded from the HLRs, Affected Components list, and architecture context; team assignments were derived from architecture-context owning teams. Epic-level acceptance criteria below were derived from the HLRs rather than the strategy's ACs.\n84\t- **Latent scope trap (activity-data surface)**: the strategy asserts the notebook controller's last-activity data merely needs surfacing. `notebooks.md` confirms activity tracking exists (per-kernel, via Jupyter server API probes) but documents no Notebook-CR-status surface for it, and `dashboard.md` states the console uses the Kubernetes API only. If implementation-time discovery finds no Kubernetes-API-readable activity surface, scope expands into the Notebooks component (Workbenches team) to expose it — that would warrant a re-plan, not a silent stretch of E001.\n85\t- **Docs epic ownership unconfirmed**: with no Impacted Teams table, E002 is assigned to the feature team (RHOAI Dashboard); confirm whether a documentation team owns the topic instead.\n86\t- **Re-split trigger for E001**: two report integrations (notebook activity, KFP run metadata) plus CSV export in one epic is at the upper end of a sprint of work; it is kept as one epic because both reports share the same console surface and the export spans both. Re-split along workbench-report vs. pipeline-run-report lines if the integration work exceeds one sprint.\n87\t- **No priority inversions detected**: P1 reports before P2 export/docs is consistent with value; the P2 export is bundled (see matrix) and docs follow the build.\n88\t\n89\t## Tiered Delivery\n90\t\n91\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all sources are\n92\tin-platform GA components.\n93\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a14d66e16020ed8a","agent_id":"a299a5fdbdfc8e4e7","session_id":"a5b399fb-2abb-4e32-b670-8f935a1667d4","uuid":"133a14c9-7a4e-422b-aa80-60ad74c25950","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:49:58.616Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba8632c9453553ab","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
