{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba34f2f7c837808f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n3\ttitle: Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers per-project idle-resource reporting in the RHOAI web console:\n34\ta report of idle workbenches (with last activity, owner, and reserved resources)\n35\tand a report of stale pipeline runs (completed runs older than a configurable\n36\tage, with retained artifacts). Administrators can export either report as CSV so\n37\tthey can reclaim capacity with confidence. All source data already exists in the\n38\tplatform — the notebook controller's activity tracking and Kubeflow Pipelines\n39\trun metadata — so this epic surfaces it in the console without code changes to\n40\tthose components.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Per-project idle-workbench report in the console: per workbench, show last\n45\t  activity (sourced from the notebook controller's activity tracking), owner,\n46\t  and reserved resources (volumes, reservations).\n47\t- Stale pipeline-run report in the console: completed pipeline runs older than a\n48\t  configurable age, with their retained artifacts, sourced from Kubeflow\n49\t  Pipelines run metadata.\n50\t- Configurable age threshold for pipeline-run staleness.\n51\t- CSV export of either report.\n52\t- Discover and consume the notebook-controller activity data and the Kubeflow\n53\t  Pipelines run metadata through surfaces the console can read (the console uses\n54\t  the Kubernetes API; it owns no data plane).\n55\t- Out of scope: automated reclamation or deletion of idle resources, and\n56\t  cost/chargeback calculations.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Given a project containing workbenches with differing activity, the console\n61\t  shows a per-project idle-workbench report listing each workbench's last\n62\t  activity, owner, and reserved resources, with last activity sourced from the\n63\t  notebook controller's activity tracking.\n64\t- Given a project with completed pipeline runs, the console shows a stale\n65\t  pipeline-run report listing completed runs older than the configured age with\n66\t  their retained artifacts, sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n67\t- The stale-run age threshold is configurable.\n68\t- Given either report, an administrator can export it as CSV.\n69\t- The notebook controller and Kubeflow Pipelines operate without code changes\n70\t  for this reporting (passive validation): the reports read their data through\n71\t  Kubernetes-API-accessible surfaces, and existing console views of workbenches\n72\t  and pipeline runs continue to work.\n73\t- No automated reclamation/deletion or cost/chargeback functionality is\n74\t  introduced.\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability\n77\t\n78\t- HLR-1 (P1): per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner, reserved\n79\t  resources) sourced from notebook controller activity tracking.\n80\t- HLR-2 (P1): stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a\n81\t  configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run\n82\t  metadata.\n83\t- HLR-3 (P2, bundled): CSV export of either report — bundled because it renders\n84\t  the same report data through the same report views; not separately\n85\t  schedulable.\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a14d66e16020ed8a","agent_id":"a299a5fdbdfc8e4e7","session_id":"a5b399fb-2abb-4e32-b670-8f935a1667d4","uuid":"6120b17e-eaa8-41e7-a4d6-b480ddc2b167","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:50:01.604Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba34f2f7c837808f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
