epo-onboarding epics exist, so Rules 7/8/10 parallelism is trivially satisfied. No branch files, no circular or invalid edges. Critical path length 2 fits the S-strategy heuristic (1-2). Cross-check of epic content found no uncaptured data/artifact dependencies: the notebook-controller and KFP data sources are in-platform components (not epics), and E002's consumption of the implemented capability is captured by the existing edge.\n25\t\n26\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n27\tE001 (Dashboard / RHOAI Dashboard) and E002 (Documentation / RHOAI Dashboard) are correctly separated by work-product type (code vs. content authoring) per the type-mixing rule. No cross-team bundling; team assignments match `dashboard.md`'s owning team, with the docs-ownership uncertainty honestly recorded as a health warning. No scope duplication — E002 documents E001's surface, it does not rebuild it. E001's size (two report integrations plus CSV export) is at the upper end of a sprint, but the summary records a concrete re-split trigger in Health Warnings (\"re-split along workbench-report vs. pipeline-run-report lines if the integration work exceeds one sprint\") — a managed watch item per the oversized-epic handling rule, not a defect.\n28\t\n29\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n30\tBoth epics are correctly typed Implementation (E001 general, E002 `docs-authoring`). No Investigation epics — justified: the strategy declares \"Open Questions: None\", and the one latent unknown (the console-readable surface for notebook activity data) is handled as an acceptance criterion on E001 with the expansion risk recorded as a health warning and re-plan trigger rather than silently absorbed. That handling is consistent and on the record. No `gated_by` fields exist and no epic depends on an Investigation, so the gating-metadata checks are vacuously satisfied. Both epics produce concrete artifacts (console reports; documentation topics).\n31\t\n32\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n33\tType-appropr